@startuml
!include style.iuml
title Organization - preview, consent, and initial batch
start
:Choose a valid Downloads Folder\nand Organization Policy;
:Reconcile any interrupted Operations;
:Inspect eligible, ready top-level files;
:Classify and propose available names;\nremember content in a Preview;
note right
  Zero proposals is valid.
  Preview creates no category folders
  and moves no new download files.
end note
:Inspect Preview and request organization;
if (Policy still matches Preview?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Request a fresh Preview;
  stop
endif
if (Consent given for this folder?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Leave downloads untouched;\nmonitoring remains paused;
  stop
endif
while (Another Organization Proposal?) is (yes)
  :Recheck eligibility and readiness;
  if (Still eligible and ready?) then (yes)
    if (Content changed since Preview?) then (yes)
      :Reject stale proposal;\nrequest fresh Preview;
      stop
    else (no)
    endif
    :Re-evaluate rule and available name;
    if (Preparation failed or canceled?) then (yes)
      :Stop startup; no new Operation;
      stop
    else (no)
    endif
    :Record Organize as Pending;
    :Attempt verified no-overwrite move;
    if (Move and facts confirmed?) then (yes)
      :Complete Operation; record Organized;\nset firstOrganizedAt;
    else (no)
      :Record Failed or NeedsAttention;\nreport error; preserve evidence;
      stop
    endif
  else (no)
    :Skip this candidate for now;
  endif
endwhile (no)
:Start monitoring under the same consent;
stop
legend bottom
  Future and unfinished arrivals use the same per-file rules under this consent, without a new Preview.
  Background errors are reported; unrelated files can still be processed.
endlegend
@enduml
